ts:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a - b}{a + b} = \\frac{\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2}\\right)}{\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2}\\right)}\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\), we substitute \\(\\alpha = \\pi - \\beta - \\gamma\\) into the tangent theorem. This gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a - b}{a + b} = \\frac{\\tan\\left( \\frac{\\pi - 2\\beta - \\gamma}{2} \\right)}{\\tan\\left( \\frac{\\pi - \\gamma}{2} \\right)}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the arguments of the tangent functions, we use the identity \\(\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - x\\right) = \\cot x\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a - b}{a + b} = \\frac{\\tan\\left( \\frac{\\pi - \\gamma}{2} - \\beta \\right)}{\\cot \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a - b}{a + b} = \\tan\\left( \\frac{\\pi - \\gamma}{2} - \\beta \\right) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity \\(\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - x\\right) = \\cot x\\), we rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[\n\\cot\\left( \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + \\beta \\right) = \\frac{a - b}{(a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}\n\\]\n\nTaking reciprocals and applying the tangent addition formula:\n\n\\[\n\\tan\\left( \\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\right) = \\frac{(a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{a - b}\n\\]\n\nUsing the tangent addition formula \\(\\tan(\\theta + \\phi) = \\frac{\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\phi}{1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\phi}\\) and solving for \\(\\tan \\beta\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{1 - \\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}} = \\frac{(a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{a - b}\n\\]\n\nLetting \\(T = \\tan \\beta\\) and \\(t = \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\), we solve the equation:\n\n\\[\nT = \\frac{2b t}{(a - b) + (a + b) t^2}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting back, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\beta = \\frac{2b \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{(a + b) \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a - b)}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final formula is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\operatorname{tg} \\beta=\\frac{2 b \\operatorname{tg} \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{(a+b) \\operatorname{tg}^{2} \\frac{\\gamma}{2}+(a-b)}}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\nWe start with the given tangens-t\u00e9tel (tangent theorem):\n\n\\[ \\frac{a+b}{a-b} = \\frac{\\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2}}{\\tan \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2}} \\]\n\nWe know the following angle relationships:\n\\[ \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} = 90^\\circ - \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2} = 90^\\circ - \\left(\\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\right) \\]\n\nFrom these relationships, we replace the arguments of tangent functions with their cotangent counterparts:\n\\[ \\frac{a+b}{a-b} = \\frac{\\cot \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{\\cot\\left(\\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\right)} \\]\n\nNext, we convert the cotangent terms back into tangent terms using the identity \\(\\cot(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{\\tan(\\theta)}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{a+b}{\\frac{1}{\\tan\\left(\\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\right)}} = \\frac{a-b}{\\frac{1}{\\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}} \\]\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\left(\\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\right) = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nWe can continue by using the tangent addition formula:\n\\[ \\tan \\left(\\beta + \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{1 - \\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}} \\]\n\nSubstitute this into our equation:\n\\[ (a+b) \\frac{\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{1 - \\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nMultiply both sides of the equation by the denominator \\(1 - \\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}\\):\n\\[ (a+b) (\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}) = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} (1 - \\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}) \\]\n\nDistribute the terms:\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nRearrange the terms to isolate \\(\\tan \\beta\\):\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nBring the terms involving \\(\\tan \\beta\\) to one side:\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nCombine the \\(\\tan \\beta\\) terms:\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta + (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nFactor out \\(\\tan \\beta\\):\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a-b) \\tan \\beta = (a+b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} - (a-b) \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\n\\[ (a+b) \\tan \\beta \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a-b) \\tan \\beta = 2b \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nFactor out \\(\\tan \\beta\\) on the left-hand side:\n\\[ \\tan \\beta \\left[(a+b) \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a-b)\\right] = 2b \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, solve for \\(\\tan \\beta\\):\n\\[ \\tan \\beta = \\frac{2b \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{(a+b) \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a-b)} \\]\n\nThus, we have shown that:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\tan \\beta = \\frac{2b \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2}}{(a+b) \\tan^2 \\frac{\\gamma}{2} + (a-b)}} \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "A sealed horizontal cylindrical vessel of length \\( l \\) is divided into two parts by a movable partition. On one side of the partition, there is 1 mole of oxygen, and on the other side, there is 1 mole of helium and 1 mole of oxygen, with the partition being initially in equilibrium. At a certain moment, the partition becomes permeable to helium but remains impermeable to oxygen. Find the displacement of the partition. The temperatures of the gases are the same a