 a^2 + b^2 - 2ac - 2bd) = u + v - (v + u - 2ac - 2bd) = 2ac + 2bd.\n\nSo, U = 2ec + 2fd, V = 2ea + 2fb, W = 2ac + 2bd.\n\nSo U, V, W are linear in coordinates. Hmm, maybe we can substitute these expressions into the equation to be proved.\n\nThe equation is:\n\nuU\u00b2 + vV\u00b2 + wW\u00b2 = UVW + 4uvw.\n\nLet me compute each term step by step.\n\nFirst, let's compute uU\u00b2:\n\nu = AD\u00b2 = a\u00b2 + b\u00b2.\n\nU = 2ec + 2fd. So U\u00b2 = (2ec + 2fd)^2 = 4e\u00b2c\u00b2 + 8ecfd + 4f\u00b2d\u00b2.\n\nMultiply by u: uU\u00b2 = (a\u00b2 + b\u00b2)(4e\u00b2c\u00b2 + 8ecfd + 4f\u00b2d\u00b2).\n\nSimilarly, compute vV\u00b2:\n\nv = BD\u00b2 = c\u00b2 + d\u00b2.\n\nV = 2ea + 2fb. V\u00b2 = (2ea + 2fb)^2 = 4e\u00b2a\u00b2 + 8eafb + 4f\u00b2b\u00b2.\n\nMultiply by v: vV\u00b2 = (c\u00b2 + d\u00b2)(4e\u00b2a\u00b2 + 8eafb + 4f\u00b2b\u00b2).\n\nSimilarly, compute wW\u00b2:\n\nw = CD\u00b2 = e\u00b2 + f\u00b2.\n\nW = 2ac + 2bd. W\u00b2 = (2ac + 2bd)^2 = 4a\u00b2c\u00b2 + 8acbd + 4b\u00b2d\u00b2.\n\nMultiply by w: wW\u00b2 = (e\u00b2 + f\u00b2)(4a\u00b2c\u00b2 + 8acbd + 4b\u00b2d\u00b2).\n\nNow, sum up uU\u00b2 + vV\u00b2 + wW\u00b2. This looks very complicated. Let's see if we can expand all these terms and see if they can be simplified to match the right-hand side.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute the right-hand side: UVW + 4uvw.\n\nFirst, compute UVW:\n\nU = 2ec + 2fd,\n\nV = 2ea + 2fb,\n\nW = 2ac + 2bd.\n\nSo UVW = (2ec + 2fd)(2ea + 2fb)(2ac + 2bd). Let's factor out the 2s:\n\nUVW = 2(ec + fd) * 2(ea + fb) * 2(ac + bd) = 8(ec + fd)(ea + fb)(ac + bd).\n\nSo UVW = 8(ec + fd)(ea + fb)(ac + bd).\n\nThen, 4uvw: u = a\u00b2 + b\u00b2, v = c\u00b2 + d\u00b2, w = e\u00b2 + f\u00b2. So 4uvw = 4(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2)(c\u00b2 + d\u00b2)(e\u00b2 + f\u00b2).\n\nSo the right-hand side is 8(ec + fd)(ea + fb)(ac + bd) + 4(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2)(c\u00b2 + d\u00b2)(e\u00b2 + f\u00b2).\n\nThis seems quite involved. Comparing the left-hand side and the right-hand side, both are expressions in 